  "body": "Part of #1446. Follow-up of #1489.\n\nWhat is missing: the 2D Pocket page has no \"Rest machining\" group. #1489 added the parameter (`OpParams::Pocket { rest }`), the undoable edit, the project-file key and the MCP parameters. The page passes the group through unchanged on Apply, but a user cannot see the group or set it in the GUI.\n\nWanted: a \"Rest machining\" group on the 2D Pocket page. It has an on/off switch (default off) and fields for the previous tool diameter, the previous tool's corner radius, the stock that the previous operation left on the walls, and the rest allowance. Apply goes through EditOperationParams, so the refusals of #1489 come back on Apply by name. The structural twin assertions cover the group. Before/after screenshots go in the PR.\n\nDone means: the group shows on a 2D Pocket and turns rest machining on and off; undo restores it; a previous tool that is not larger is refused by name on Apply.",
